From e2ac131b352bebaf746a2eb2ea923b665fbe43ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:46:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(kanban): explicit placement='auto' beats a
 context skill's local marker; remedy names 'auto'

The local-marker remedy told callers to re-create with placement='hub', but hub
admission refuses portable work and creates nothing, leaving an archived card and
no replacement (t_01a1cfbd8f74bf87, skill myapp-development).

- An explicit placement='auto' drops context skill markers (^myapp, ^bb-;
  kanban.placement.auto_overridable_skill_markers replaces the list) from the
  local-marker scan (kanban_placement.marker_skills), so the card queues for
  pool:worker. Device-bound skills (apple-*, computer-use, macos-, ios-, a local
  Chrome) still pin, since 'auto' is also the routine default callers spell out.
  An omitted placement still keeps every skill-marker card local. Title/body
  markers are unchanged.
- Remedies (kanban_placement.marker_remedy): context skill -> re-create with
  placement='auto'; device skill -> re-create without the skill; text marker ->
  drop the machine from the title/body. KANBAN_GUIDANCE and the kanban_archive
  schema now point at placement.remedy instead of placement='hub'.
- The local-pin 'would run elsewhere' note simulates an omitted placement, not
  an explicit 'auto' (tested).
